SW09 -- the mean-value structure. (T1) <g_N>_Omega = g_env(B) exactly: the
enclosed baryons average to zero (ANY interior configuration), the environment
contributes its centre value. (T2) eta = |g_env(B)|/a0 is a POINT value -- all
the nonlocality sits in Gamma, none in eta. (T3) Gamma = RMS deviation from
the ambient. DC/AC split (P10): the DC part goes to eta (conformal suppression,
shape preserved); the AC/tidal part goes to Gamma (shape distortion, no
suppression -- a symmetric external pair gives eta = 0 exactly while moving
Gamma). Retro-justification: SW01b's eta_sun = v_c^2/R_0/a0 = 2.292 is exactly
|g_env(B)|/a0. MUTATE: the hinge localises at the field point P and fails by the tidal variation -- non-vacuous.

